# The lines the Slang twin of default/main.vert may declare differently from the GLSL (task 0072, stage f), read by
# SlangPermutations in components-tests: "[<define set>] glsl-only: <line>"; every listed line must occur, so a stale
# entry fails the test. All of them are declarations the GLSL keeps and never reads (glslang keeps them, slangc drops
# them); a pipeline may supply attributes and bindings a shader does not read, so nothing the pipeline builds changes.
# Specialization constants that nothing reads (texmatUv without TEXMAT) need no line (vsgUtil::readSpirvInterface).
#
# MORPH: the vertex position input (location 0); the positions come from the morph buffer.
# PARTICLE without NORMAL: the point light buffers (set 0, bindings 2 to 5), which only the vertex lighting of NORMAL reads.
#   (The scene uniform, binding 0, is read since task 0359 stage b: the analytic particles take the scene time.)
[COLOR MORPH NORMAL TEXCOORD UVSETS_1 VERTEX] glsl-only: in location=0 vec3f32
[MORPH NORMAL TEXCOORD UVSETS_1 VERTEX] glsl-only: in location=0 vec3f32
[PARTICLE SOFT_PARTICLE UVSETS_1] glsl-only: descriptor set=0 binding=2 storage 0:runtime_array stride32;0:vec4f32;16:vec4f32;
[PARTICLE SOFT_PARTICLE UVSETS_1] glsl-only: descriptor set=0 binding=3 storage 0:runtime_array stride4;0:u32;
[PARTICLE SOFT_PARTICLE UVSETS_1] glsl-only: descriptor set=0 binding=4 storage 0:runtime_array stride8;0:u32;4:u32;
[PARTICLE SOFT_PARTICLE UVSETS_1] glsl-only: descriptor set=0 binding=5 uniform 0:u32;4:u32;8:u32;12:u32;
[PARTICLE UVSETS_1] glsl-only: descriptor set=0 binding=2 storage 0:runtime_array stride32;0:vec4f32;16:vec4f32;
[PARTICLE UVSETS_1] glsl-only: descriptor set=0 binding=3 storage 0:runtime_array stride4;0:u32;
[PARTICLE UVSETS_1] glsl-only: descriptor set=0 binding=4 storage 0:runtime_array stride8;0:u32;4:u32;
[PARTICLE UVSETS_1] glsl-only: descriptor set=0 binding=5 uniform 0:u32;4:u32;8:u32;12:u32;
